{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "If you have been programming in Rails for pretty much any length of time, you will definitely run into a method that looks like this:", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ada68d7f54d1e9a7e864d1a91bc75cde5fed9f868544cb3ebc9d7007fd2bee69.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.42], [7, 1.42, 1.76], [8, 1.76, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.32], [10, 2.32, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.86], [12, 2.86, 3.04], [13, 3.04, 3.36], [14, 3.86, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.04], [16, 4.04, 4.4], [17, 4.4, 4.74], [18, 4.74, 5.0], [19, 5.0, 5.12], [20, 5.12, 5.38], [21, 5.38, 5.58], [22, 5.58, 5.74], [23, 5.74, 5.98], [24, 5.98, 6.24]]}, {"text": "You initiate some local variable, do some things to it, then return it.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7b3247d616f0d01d17cdce8f536df4518d7ee48aeec66563f2db2c9dbfc7fa70.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.22, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.14], [4, 1.14, 1.6], [5, 2.04, 2.14], [6, 2.14, 2.34], [7, 2.34, 2.56], [8, 2.56, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 2.94], [10, 3.04, 3.16], [11, 3.16, 3.44], [12, 3.44, 3.7]]}, {"text": "There is a lot of boiler plate code here and the smart developers behind rails added a method to the object class called returning.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/722ffb811edde0a0daa9f26f1c92aa4bdf2cb2710b56eb18697fe0af4e44c9d0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 1.02], [7, 1.6, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.22], [10, 2.62, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 2.98], [12, 2.98, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.94], [14, 3.94, 4.42], [15, 4.42, 5.22], [16, 5.22, 5.38], [17, 5.38, 5.64], [18, 5.64, 5.88], [19, 5.88, 6.0], [20, 6.0, 6.24], [21, 6.24, 6.62], [22, 6.62, 7.04], [23, 7.04, 7.56]]}, {"text": "This method simplifies this workflow.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/92e3a9bf6433dec9a93a1f5579a83734022b23c2cf72ffdc7b8699c2e8789818.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 1.3], [3, 1.3, 1.52], [4, 1.52, 1.86]]}, {"text": "Here is an example of the returning method in action.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/75fd2a1729b5eb590c843e9fce12d248d14cf9be1fef375308bd55dc54518c32.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.44, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.62], [7, 1.62, 1.94], [8, 1.94, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.4]]}, {"text": "This is a much more elegant solution since it just reads more like a sentence than the previous example.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1f34179dcd285dfc8cf7ed473048311fbb942768de12f73b368710c4a0291772.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 1.14], [6, 1.14, 1.68], [7, 1.68, 1.98], [8, 1.98, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 2.96], [12, 2.96, 3.14], [13, 3.14, 3.28], [14, 3.28, 3.54], [15, 3.54, 3.88], [16, 3.88, 4.0], [17, 4.0, 4.3], [18, 4.3, 4.76]]}, {"text": "“Add Cat and Dog to foo then return” vs “create foo.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6d7b907dd1db4c31b3307256cea65e12546757bba094a9224bde18693d4d63a4.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.26, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.74], [6, 1.74, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.44], [9, 3.24, 3.8], [10, 3.8, 4.36]]}, {"text": "Add Cat and Dog.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1db76dd0b37cd0e2447d973169a4d24bb8b909d296d37fbb43960f7493cf1f75.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [2, 0.78, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.14]]}, {"text": "return foo”.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/40959d7b8fe70718d8c2c5db771a2481a381a41a46fe8c35b622b98a0453f433.mp3"}, {"text": "Ruby’s ability to easily add DSL to objectss on the fly makes ruby so powerful and easy to maintian.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7bd4b47738925ed2c5c0236a00a9468df8f9d29879af7a70e61381fecfb2b8b7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.82], [2, 0.82, 1.06], [3, 1.06, 1.46], [4, 1.46, 1.72], [5, 1.72, 2.24], [6, 2.24, 2.4], [8, 3.02, 3.28], [9, 3.28, 3.38], [10, 3.38, 3.62], [11, 3.62, 3.84], [12, 3.84, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.38], [14, 4.38, 4.88], [15, 4.88, 5.18], [16, 5.18, 5.48], [17, 5.48, 5.66]]}]}